  "license_note": "Class codes and names from the BKG documentation (Anlage 1). The documentation prints only colour names for the LB groups (A pink, B yellow, C light green, D dark green, E grey, F violet, G light blue), so no colours are given.",
  "key": "lb",
  "fields": {"lb": ["lb_akt", "landbedeckung"], "ln": ["ln_akt", "landnutzung"], "zus": ["zus_akt"]},
  "note": "Each LBM-DE polygon has a land-cover code (LB_AKT, Bxxx) and a land-use code (LN_AKT, Nxxx); minimum mapping unit 1 ha. With both codes, the combination entries decide where the use changes the drawing (built-up cover by use; grassland in urban green, sport, traffic, residential or extensive use; open ground in extraction, dumps or building sites; ZUS_AKT F = Friedhof, S = Solar). Otherwise the land cover (lb) wins over the use (ln), because lb entries come first. LBM-DE codes are not the codes of the AdV schemas Landbedeckung/Landnutzung (see adv_lbln).",
